**collect(Collector) — the most powerful terminal:**

```java
// To List:
List<String> symbols = trades.stream().map(Trade::getSymbol).collect(Collectors.toList());
List<String> symbols2 = trades.stream().map(Trade::getSymbol).toList();  // Java 16 (unmodifiable!)

// To Set:
Set<String> unique = trades.stream().map(Trade::getSymbol).collect(Collectors.toSet());

// To Map:
Map<String, BigDecimal> symbolToAmount = trades.stream()
    .collect(Collectors.toMap(Trade::getSymbol, Trade::getAmount));

// Grouping:
Map<String, List<Trade>> bySymbol = trades.stream()
    .collect(Collectors.groupingBy(Trade::getSymbol));

// Joining:
String csv = trades.stream().map(Trade::getSymbol)
    .collect(Collectors.joining(", "));  // "RELIANCE, TCS, HDFC"

// Partitioning:
Map<Boolean, List<Trade>> settled = trades.stream()
    .collect(Collectors.partitioningBy(Trade::isSettled));
// {true: [settled trades], false: [unsettled trades]}

// Summarizing:
DoubleSummaryStatistics stats = trades.stream()
    .collect(Collectors.summarizingDouble(t -> t.getAmount().doubleValue()));
// stats.getSum(), stats.getAverage(), stats.getMax(), stats.getMin(), stats.getCount()
```

**reduce(identity, BinaryOperator) — fold into single value:**

```java
// Sum amounts:
BigDecimal total = trades.stream()
    .map(Trade::getAmount)
    .reduce(BigDecimal.ZERO, BigDecimal::add);  // identity=0, accumulator=add

// Find max (without Comparator):
Optional<BigDecimal> max = trades.stream()
    .map(Trade::getAmount)
    .reduce(BigDecimal::max);  // no identity → returns Optional

// Concatenate symbols:
String all = Stream.of("RELIANCE", "TCS", "HDFC")
    .reduce("", (a, b) -> a.isEmpty() ? b : a + ", " + b);
```

**forEach(Consumer) — fire-and-forget action:**

```java
trades.stream().forEach(t -> auditService.log(t));  // side-effect
trades.forEach(t -> auditService.log(t));            // Collection.forEach — NOT stream!
// ⚠ In parallel streams, forEach order is NOT guaranteed!
// Use forEachOrdered() if order matters in parallel.
```

**count() — count elements (triggers full pipeline):**

```java
long settled = trades.stream().filter(Trade::isSettled).count();
```

**findFirst() / findAny() — short-circuit:**

```java
Optional<Trade> first = trades.stream()
    .filter(Trade::isSettled)
    .findFirst();  // first in encounter order → stops pipeline!

Optional<Trade> any = trades.parallelStream()
    .filter(Trade::isSettled)
    .findAny();  // faster in parallel — any thread's first match
```

**anyMatch / allMatch / noneMatch — short-circuit boolean:**

```java
boolean hasFraud = trades.stream().anyMatch(t -> t.getAmount().compareTo(limit) > 0);
// First true → returns true, STOPS

boolean allValid = trades.stream().allMatch(Trade::isSettled);
// First false → returns false, STOPS

boolean noFailed = trades.stream().noneMatch(t -> "FAILED".equals(t.getStatus()));
// First true → returns false, STOPS
```

